WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.758
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Intermediate.

2
00:00:05.058 --> 00:00:08.270
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:14.497
Unit six: Living with Technology. In this unit, you will talk about technology habits and digital life.

4
00:00:15.483 --> 00:00:17.018
notification overload.

5
00:00:17.718 --> 00:00:22.226
notification overload means receiving too many alerts on your phone or computer.

6
00:00:22.526 --> 00:00:25.698
Notification overload makes it hard to concentrate.

7
00:00:26.398 --> 00:00:29.817
Your turn. Say: notification overload.

8
00:00:32.517 --> 00:00:34.295
notification overload.

9
00:00:35.283 --> 00:00:36.668
digital detox.

10
00:00:37.368 --> 00:00:41.492
digital detox means a period of time without using phones or computers.

11
00:00:41.792 --> 00:00:44.418
I did a weekend digital detox in the countryside.

12
00:00:45.118 --> 00:00:47.712
Your turn. Say: digital detox.

13
00:00:50.412 --> 00:00:51.832
digital detox.

14
00:00:52.817 --> 00:00:53.945
cloud storage.

15
00:00:54.645 --> 00:00:58.688
cloud storage means saving files on the internet instead of on your device.

16
00:00:58.988 --> 00:01:01.255
All my photos are backed up in cloud storage.

17
00:01:01.955 --> 00:01:04.456
Your turn. Say: cloud storage.

18
00:01:07.156 --> 00:01:08.378
cloud storage.

19
00:01:09.383 --> 00:01:10.593
smart speaker.

20
00:01:11.293 --> 00:01:14.454
smart speaker means a speaker you can control with your voice.

21
00:01:14.754 --> 00:01:17.462
Our smart speaker plays music when I ask it to.

22
00:01:18.162 --> 00:01:20.605
Your turn. Say: smart speaker.

23
00:01:23.305 --> 00:01:24.527
smart speaker.

24
00:01:25.517 --> 00:01:26.808
cyber security.

25
00:01:27.508 --> 00:01:31.226
cyber security means protecting computers and data from attacks.

26
00:01:31.526 --> 00:01:34.199
Banks spend a lot of money on cyber security.

27
00:01:34.899 --> 00:01:37.563
Your turn. Say: cyber security.

28
00:01:40.263 --> 00:01:41.717
cyber security.

29
00:01:42.717 --> 00:01:43.927
password manager.

30
00:01:44.627 --> 00:01:48.588
password manager means an app that stores all your passwords safely.

31
00:01:48.888 --> 00:01:52.641
A password manager helps you use different passwords.

32
00:01:53.341 --> 00:01:55.935
Your turn. Say: password manager.

33
00:01:58.635 --> 00:02:00.124
password manager.

34
00:02:01.117 --> 00:02:02.106
tech support.

35
00:02:02.806 --> 00:02:06.977
tech support means help from experts when a device or program has a problem.

36
00:02:07.277 --> 00:02:10.240
I called tech support because my laptop wouldn't start.

37
00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:13.047
Your turn. Say: tech support.

38
00:02:15.747 --> 00:02:16.817
tech support.

39
00:02:17.817 --> 00:02:19.085
screen time report.

40
00:02:19.785 --> 00:02:22.806
screen time report means a summary of how long you used your phone.

41
00:02:23.106 --> 00:02:26.441
My screen time report says I used my phone for six hours!

42
00:02:27.141 --> 00:02:30.165
Your turn. Say: screen time report.

43
00:02:32.865 --> 00:02:34.295
screen time report.

44
00:02:35.283 --> 00:02:37.411
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:37.711 --> 00:02:40.003
Nita, you look worried. What's wrong?

46
00:02:41.317 --> 00:02:45.383
My laptop has been crashing all morning, and I've lost some files.

47
00:02:46.683 --> 00:02:48.799
Have you been saving them in cloud storage?

48
00:02:50.083 --> 00:02:53.247
No, I haven't. I've been meaning to set it up for weeks.

49
00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:57.641
Call tech support, and then try a digital detox this weekend.

50
00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:02.694
Good idea. My screen time report has been terrible lately!

51
00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:07.492
Grammar focus: Present perfect continuous.

52
00:03:07.792 --> 00:03:12.926
Use the present perfect continuous for an activity that started in the past and continues now.

53
00:03:13.226 --> 00:03:15.261
We often use it with for and since.

54
00:03:15.561 --> 00:03:18.791
For example: I have been using this phone for three years.

55
00:03:19.091 --> 00:03:23.865
Use it to focus on the activity and how long it has continued, often with for and since.

56
00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:27.468
Now read and listen. Are We Too Connected?.

57
00:03:27.768 --> 00:03:30.847
The average person checks their phone more than ninety times a day.

58
00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:36.321
Many people have been suffering from notification overload without realising it.

59
00:03:37.617 --> 00:03:41.613
Some workers have started a weekly digital detox to protect their focus.

60
00:03:42.917 --> 00:03:46.820
Experts also recommend checking your screen time report every week.

61
00:03:48.117 --> 00:03:52.171
Technology is useful, but we need to control it, not let it control us.

62
00:03:53.483 --> 00:03:55.973
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:56.273 --> 00:03:59.120
A period without phones or computers is a blank.

64
00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:03.921
A, digital detox. B, smart speaker. C, cloud storage.

65
00:04:07.917 --> 00:04:10.357
The answer is A: digital detox.

66
00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:14.105
I blank English since 2020.

67
00:04:14.405 --> 00:04:17.617
A, have been learning. B, am learning. C, learned.

68
00:04:21.617 --> 00:04:23.709
The answer is A: have been learning.

69
00:04:25.217 --> 00:04:26.531
How long blank waiting?

70
00:04:26.831 --> 00:04:29.776
A, are you. B, have you been. C, did you.

71
00:04:33.783 --> 00:04:35.829
The answer is B: have you been.

72
00:04:37.317 --> 00:04:40.245
An app that stores passwords safely is a blank.

73
00:04:40.545 --> 00:04:45.685
A, tech support. B, password manager. C, screen time report.

74
00:04:49.683 --> 00:04:52.089
The answer is B: password manager.

75
00:04:53.583 --> 00:04:56.372
According to the text, people check their phones blank.

76
00:04:56.672 --> 00:05:01.568
A, about nine times a day. B, more than ninety times a day. C, once an hour.

77
00:05:05.583 --> 00:05:08.512
The answer is B: more than ninety times a day.

78
00:05:10.017 --> 00:05:14.109
Now it's your turn to speak. How has technology changed your daily life?

79
00:05:19.409 --> 00:05:23.579
I've been using online banking for two years, so I rarely carry cash now.

80
00:05:23.879 --> 00:05:25.414
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:26.417 --> 00:05:30.752
Great work today! You learned eight new words and present perfect continuous.

82
00:05:31.052 --> 00:05:34.552
Today's value is good habits. Do good things every day.

83
00:05:34.852 --> 00:05:37.029
See you in Unit seven. Goodbye!

84
00:05:37.329 --> 00:05:39.946
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

